## Development

Requires [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/), [just](https://just.systems/) and a
C++{{ cpp_standard }} compiler. CMake, Ninja, clang-format, clang-tidy and gcovr are
installed into the project environment by `uv sync`; clangd (for editors and
Claude) and ccache are optional system packages. `just doctor` reports what is missing.

```sh
just setup   # create the environment (builds the extension), configure the dev build, install git hooks
just check   # format check, lint, type check, C++ and Python tests
just         # list every recipe
```

| Task | Python | C++ |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Build and dependencies | uv, scikit-build-core | CMake presets, Ninja, CPM.cmake |
| Format and lint | ruff | clang-format, clang-tidy |
| Type check | ty | - |
| Tests and coverage | pytest, pytest-cov | Catch2, gcovr, ASan + UBSan |
| Docs | MkDocs Material, mkdocstrings | - |

Git hooks run through prek. The repository carries Claude Code settings
(`CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/`): edits are auto-formatted, `just check` runs before
Claude finishes a task, and the Astral and `clangd-lsp` plugins provide the ty
and clangd language servers.
